course: dictionary
lesson: 10465
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word tube is a good example. In «It squeezes about 70 to 100 times a minute and pumps blood through tubes called blood vessels», a tube is a long, hollow pipe that blood can flow through.
explain: Now try a different sentence: «Squeeze the paint out of the tube.» Here a tube is a soft container that you press to get the paint out. The clues are the words squeeze and paint, not the word tube itself.
explain: Capital letters can be a clue too. «Take the Tube to school» has a capital T, so it means the underground railway in London. Always ask what word would fit, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A tube is a long, hollow pipe that liquid or air can go through.
fact: The small intestine is a tube about six metres (about 20 feet) long, folded up in your belly.
fact: The heart pumps blood through tubes called blood vessels.
fact: The Tube, with a capital T, is the underground railway in London.
fact: On the TV, "on the tube" is an informal phrase, mostly used in America and Australia.
exercise: «Owl eyes are fixed like tubes, so owls turn their heads instead.» What shape are owl eyes compared to? | Triangles | *Tubes | Flat plates | Balls that roll
exercise: Liam says, «I take the Tube to school every day.» What does the Tube mean here? | A soft container you squeeze | A swim ring | A long hollow pipe for liquid | *The underground railway in London
exercise: In science, the teacher fills a small test tube with water. What is a test tube? | A ring you float on | A soft container for toothpaste | The underground railway | *A small tube that holds small amounts of liquid in an experiment
test: In «Mum squeezed the last of the glue from its tube», what is a tube? | A swim ring | The underground railway in London | *A soft container you squeeze | A long hollow pipe
test: «The Tube was packed at rush hour.» What is the Tube? | A lab pipe | *The underground railway in London | A soft container | A TV programme
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Blood vessels are tubes that carry blood to every part of the body»? | A soft container you squeeze | *A long hollow pipe for blood | A TV show | The underground railway in London
